Subject: [PATCH 2/3] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 4, patch 2;
 built on f9e70c167 with series 2 and 3 applied): NOTHING IN THE ENVIRONMENT
 MOVES A GATE -- GIT'S OWN VARIABLES (a further form of main's unseen case
 U9.b, found by this seat). Git reads a few variables that send it somewhere
 else than the folder it is run in. With GIT_DIR pointing at another
 repository, an export of the tree was read as a full clone, and seven gates
 of the table passed on it, git answering for the other repository. With
 GIT_INDEX_FILE pointing at an empty index, a real clone had no tracked file,
 and the same seven passed. THE MEND: where one of five such variables is set,
 the places git reads for the folder (its git directory, its top level, its
 common directory, its index, its objects) are asked for twice, as the
 environment has it and without those variables; if they differ the folder is
 read as 'redirected', and every gate of the table is refused in plain words,
 naming the variable. A hook's environment that names the folder's own
 repository gives the same places both ways and is not refused: main's three
 tests of the push hook pass as before. The lock: two tests added to
 tests/test_gates_are_a_function_of_the_commit.py, three forms and the hook's
 case; on the commit before, the first fails naming the seven gates that pass.
 The static test of patch 1 is told of the one new read of the environment.
 Computed once; tested against planted errors, 3 of 3. 0 of 19.

